On 9/16/2014 2:38 AM, Gleki Arxokuna wrote:
> Xorlo was an unlucky part of Lojban history where the founders like
> Lojbab didnt see it as a change invalidating CLL, and the others didnt
> bother of amending books and the dictionary.

Actually I did, but I was a) greatly outvoted and b) convinced that the 
existing gadri system was broken in a way that made it undocumentable to 
BPFK standards, by the people who had accepted responsibility for doing 
so (i.e. Nick and later Robin as jatnas).

One of the few reasons for accepting a change to the baseline, was if 
CLL was incorrect or self-contradictory.  Having something that was 
fundamentally broken was another plausible reason.  The active people on 
the byfy were overwhelmingly convinced that this was the case for gadri, 
and the really tough question was as to what was the minimal change 
needed to fix things.

